Using the new CTZ64 intrinsic. 

Per [Godbolt](https://cpp.godbolt.org/z/vjKGPcWjq), turns out the fastest way to iterate the set bits is using `set &= (set - 1)` vs `set &= ~(1ULL << index)`:

```cpp
while (set != 0) {
  uint32_t index = CTZ64(set);
  // do something ...
  // Option 1
  set &= (set - 1); // clear least significant bit that is set
  // Option 2
  // set &= ~(1ULL << index);
}
```

| option | arch | loop instruction count |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | x64 | 5 |
| 2 | x64 | 8 |
| 1 | arm64 | 6 |
| 2 | arm64 | 7 |

